AIM :
To write a Python program using regular expressions (re module) to validate whether the given input is a valid email ID or a 10-digit mobile number.
Algorithm:
Start the program.
Import the re module.
Accept an email ID or mobile number from the user.
Define a regular expression pattern for validating email IDs.
Define a regular expression pattern for validating 10-digit mobile numbers.
Use re.fullmatch() to check whether the input matches the email pattern.
If it matches, display "Valid email id".
Otherwise, check whether it matches the mobile number pattern.
If it matches, display "Valid mobile no".
Otherwise, display "Invalid email or mobile no".
Stop the program.
CODE:
import re

data=input("Enter email or ph no")
email_pattern=r'^[a-zA-Z0-9.%+-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+.[a-zA-Z]{2,}$'
mobile_pattern=r'^[0-9]{10}$'
if re.fullmatch(email_pattern,data):
print("Valid email id")
elif re.fullmatch(mobile_pattern, data):
print("Valid mobile no")
else:
print("Invalid email or mobile no")

